=== Abraham
--- Abraham [title]
overline: Romans 4 • Abraham
heading: Abraham
sub: Believed God, and It Was Counted unto Him for Righteousness
refs: Genesis 15:6; Romans 4:3

--- Called Out of Ur
kicker: Abraham
step: Before age 75 (while in Ur of the Chaldees, Mesopotamia) | The God of glory appeared to Abram and gave the first promise/call. [[Genesis 12:1]]; [[Acts 7:2-3]]
step: Age unknown (but before 75) | Terah took Abram, Sarai, and Lot from Ur toward Canaan, but they settled in Haran. [[Genesis 11:31]]

--- Age 75
kicker: Abraham
step: Age 75 | After Terah’s death in Haran, God renewed the call. Abram departed Haran for Canaan with Sarai and Lot.
scripture: Genesis 12:1-3

--- Hebron and the War of the Kings
kicker: Abraham
step: Age ~75–86 | Settled near the plain of Moreh and then the oaks of Mamre at **Hebron**, building altars to the Lord. [[Genesis 12:6-9]]; [[Genesis 13:18]]
step: Age ~80–85 | Participated in the **War of the Kings**, rescuing Lot after defeating Chedorlaomer and his allies; met Melchizedek, king of Salem, and gave him tithes. [[Genesis 14:1-24|Genesis 14]]

--- Ishmael, the Covenant and Isaac
kicker: Abraham
step: Age 86 | Ishmael born to Hagar, Sarai’s Egyptian handmaid. [[Genesis 16:15-16]]
step: Age 99 | God appeared to Abram, changed his name to **Abraham** (“father of many nations”) and Sarai’s to Sarah; instituted **circumcision** as the token of the covenant. Abraham, Ishmael (age 13), and all males in his household were circumcised. [[Genesis 17:1-27]]
step: Age 100 | Isaac born to Sarah. [[Genesis 21:1-5]]

--- Moriah and Machpelah
kicker: Abraham
step: Age ~133 (Isaac ~33) | God commanded Abraham to offer Isaac as a burnt offering on Mount Moriah. Abraham obeyed, but the angel of the Lord stopped him and provided a ram instead. God renewed the covenant promises because Abraham did not withhold his son. [[Genesis 22:1-19]]; [[Hebrews 11:17-19]]
step: Age 175 | Abraham died and was buried in the cave of Machpelah near Hebron. [[Genesis 25:7-10]]

